WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.020
it's lab muffin here your resident
beauty science nerd and today we're

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.950
going to be talking about visible light
more specifically we're going to be

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:12.780
talking about blue light and what that
does to your skin we all know about UV

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.130
rays from the Sun damaging your skin and
you might have also heard of infrared

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:22.830
radiation but what about the wavelengths
of light that we can actually see will

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.359
they damage your skin how can you
protect your skin from visible light

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:39.239
let's take a closer look the Sun
produces a lot of light as well as the

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:42.719
wavelengths of light that we can see
which is called visible light

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:46.980
there's also ultraviolet or UV light
which has shorter wavelengths and higher

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:53.579
energy UV is one of the main causes of
aging skin on the other side at longer

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:59.250
wavelengths than visible light there's
low energy infrared or IR radiation the

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:04.739
energy from the Sun that we get on earth
is about three to seven percent UV 44%

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:11.100
visible light and 53% infrared even
though there's less UV in total UV ends

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.049
up causing more damage because each
individual UV particle or photon has

00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:20.670
more energy it's like being hit with a
single bullet or being hit with a bunch

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:25.080
of balled up tissues that way the same as
ten bullets but there's been more

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.560
research that's been finding that
visible and infrared wavelengths can

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.900
also cause skin damage

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.470
so why is blue light the color that
everyone's interested in and not the

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:45.110
other colors like red or yellow? most of
the time when people say blue light what

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:49.820
they really mean is blue and violet
light and the reason why these colors

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:55.060
are more damaging is because of physics
shorter wavelengths of electromagnetic

00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:00.590
radiation from the Sun have more energy
in sunlight UV has the shortest

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:05.930
wavelengths which is up to 400
nanometers visible light is longer from

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:09.619
400 to 700 nanometers so it's lower in
energy

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:14.989
infrared has longer wavelengths from 700
nanometers to 1 millimeter and out of

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:20.330
these 3 it has the lowest energy if we
zoom into the visible light region the

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:26.660
order of the colors is ROYGBIV red
orange yellow green blue indigo and

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:32.480
violet infrared is past the red end
while ultraviolet is past the violet

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:37.070
end blue and violet have the shortest
wavelengths of the visible region around

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:41.750
400 to 500 nanometers and therefore out
of all of these colors it's got the

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.340
highest energy so these colors of light
are the ones that are the most likely to

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.970
cause damage that's similar to the UV
sun damage that we've been researching

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:54.530
for years and years because of their
higher energy blue and violet light is

00:02:54.530 --> 00:03:03.560
often called HEV light which stands for
high-energy visible light

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.540
the research on the impact of blue and
visible light on your skin isn't as

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:13.700
advanced as the research on UV so it's a
bit less clear exactly how it causes

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:18.770
damage to your skin and to make it more
confusing older studies on the effects

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:23.300
of blue light aren't as valid because
the electromagnetic spectrum is a

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.500
continuous spectrum there isn't any sort
of strict divide between

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:33.380
ultraviolet and visible-light except for
what human eyes can and can't see a lot

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:38.090
of the time the lights used in the older
studies actually produce UV as well as

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:41.690
blue and violet light this means that
the effects that they found could have

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:45.410
been from the stray UV light and not
actually because of the visible blue and

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:49.430
violet light at all here's what the
research shows so far about light and

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:59.450
skin just like how UVA and UVB have
different effects on the skin different

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:03.110
parts of the visible light spectrum can
also have different effects depending on

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:07.730
their wavelength which translates to
color or energy different colors in the

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:12.290
visible light spectrum can even have
opposite effects on your skin here's

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:16.790
what the studies have found in cultured
human skin cells in in vitro studies

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:21.919
blue light caused skin cells to die
while red light had no effect in animal

00:04:21.919 --> 00:04:26.510
studies blue light slowed down skin
recovery after it was irritated while

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:31.280
red light sped it up and green and white
light didn't make a difference in people

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:35.479
with dark skin blue light increased
pigment and caused dark spots on the

00:04:35.479 --> 00:04:40.640
skin while red light didn't so far it
seems that blue and violet light are the

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.630
colors of visible light that caused the
most damage to skin and it seems like

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:49.700
they caused this damage by producing
nitric oxide free radicals these free

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.479
radicals are really reactive because
they have an unpaired electron which

00:04:53.479 --> 00:04:56.990
means that they can attack other
substances in your skin like DNA and

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:02.060
proteins I've talked about free radicals
before in my video on antioxidants that

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:05.539
I've linked in the caption below there's
a lot of different types of damage that

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:09.620
free radicals can cause they can slow
down skin cell production and they can

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:14.030
break down collagen for example so with
all this free radical damage you end up

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.469
with damaged skin that looks more uneven

00:05:16.469 --> 00:05:25.830
in texture even though both visible
light and UV light both cause skin

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:30.059
damage it's important to note that they
have different effects on your skin so

00:05:30.059 --> 00:05:34.319
you can't compare the two types of
light directly for example visible light

00:05:34.319 --> 00:05:39.809
doesn't directly damage DNA but UV does
visible light also doesn't cause the

00:05:39.809 --> 00:05:44.969
same microscopic changes in your skin
that UV does UV for example increases

00:05:44.969 --> 00:05:50.999
inflammatory interleukin 8 and tumor
necrosis factor-alpha and p53 which is a

00:05:50.999 --> 00:05:55.589
tumor protein that suppresses cancer
both UV and visible light caused

00:05:55.589 --> 00:06:00.719
pigmentation or skin darkening in people
with darker skin but the pigment caused

00:06:00.719 --> 00:06:04.709
by visible light lasts longer than the
pigment caused by the longer wavelengths

00:06:04.709 --> 00:06:10.829
of UV called UVA1 the exact color of
the pigment is also different UVA1

00:06:10.829 --> 00:06:14.519
causes your skin to get a grayish
pigment that slowly turns brown after a

00:06:14.519 --> 00:06:18.329
while but visible light causes pigment
that's brown straight away

00:06:18.329 --> 00:06:23.369
you also need different amounts or doses
of UV and visible light to have a

00:06:23.369 --> 00:06:29.490
noticeable effect on skin each particle
or photon of UV has more energy than

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:34.439
each photon of visible light so again
it's like a bullet versus a balled up

00:06:34.439 --> 00:06:39.869
tissue but the total energy to have an
effect on your skin is also different so

00:06:39.869 --> 00:06:44.249
with the tissue analogy not only do you
need enough balls of tissue to get the

00:06:44.249 --> 00:06:49.319
same weight as a bullet you actually
need a whole lot more different studies

00:06:49.319 --> 00:06:53.639
have found that you need between 8 and
30 times as much visible light as UV in

00:06:53.639 --> 00:07:03.270
terms of the units for light energy
which is joules per square centimeter

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.600
the effects of visible light also
depends on the type of skin you have in

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:11.410
terms of skin tone
in one study none of the tested

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:14.350
amounts of visible light caused
pigmentation in people with light

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:19.090
fitzpatrick II skin but people with
darker fitzpatrick IV to VI skin

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:23.710
developed more pigment the smallest
amount of visible light that causes

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:28.420
pigmentation in all of the dark-skinned
people in one study was 40 joules per

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:33.280
square centimeter this translates to
about 30 minutes of sunlight in midday

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:38.260
in summer in Texas one theory for why
visible light has different effects on

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:42.670
dark skin and light skin is that visible
light might interact with melanin to

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:52.630
form damaging free radicals the ones
that I talked about earlier so if you

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:57.010
want to protect your skin from visible
light what can you do you might have

00:07:57.010 --> 00:08:00.750
guests with mineral sunscreens that
contain zinc oxide and titanium dioxide

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:05.680
but that's not quite right
even though a lot of people call these

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:10.540
ingredients physical blockers they don't
actually work that way they mostly work

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:15.310
just like organic also called chemical
sunscreens that absorb some wavelengths

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:19.660
so even in studies where they used a
really thick layer of mineral sunscreen

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:24.490
they still didn't protect against
visible light but there are some

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:29.020
ingredients that can help iron oxide
which is used as the main pigment in

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:34.089
foundations is effective at protecting
your skin against visible light but

00:08:34.089 --> 00:08:38.200
there isn't a standard for measuring how
well any sort of product protects

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:42.219
against visible light so there isn't a
well-used measure for how well something

00:08:42.219 --> 00:08:47.550
protects against visible light like how
we have SPF for UVB and PPD for UVA

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:53.230
since visible light causes damage via
free radicals antioxidants can also soak

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:56.410
them up which I've talked about before
in another video the one that I've

00:08:56.410 --> 00:09:00.130
linked in the description one study
found that the free radicals from

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:04.420
visible light were halved when an
antioxidant mixture with vitamin E and

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:07.870
feverfew
and soy was used on people's skin and

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:13.150
just like with UV avoiding exposure to
light can work better than just using

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:15.939
skin care products you can stay in the
shade

00:09:15.939 --> 00:09:19.869
you can wear hats and clothes as well to
protect your skin from visible light

00:09:19.869 --> 00:09:24.519
damage and that's all for today's video
I hope you liked it and you learned

00:09:24.519 --> 00:09:28.359
something new next time I'll be talking
about whether or not you should be

00:09:28.359 --> 00:09:31.569
worried about skin damage from blue
light from screens like your laptop

00:09:31.569 --> 00:09:40.259
phone tablet or computer stay tuned to
find out more as always subscribe follow

